    "probe_text": "The trace is confirmed. Here is everything applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`, in exact order.\n\n## Before the controller runs (framework layer)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Requires role `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`; otherwise 403/401.\n2. **Bean Validation on the request DTO** (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`), which runs before the method body. On failure \u2192 400 via `ExceptionControllerAdvice`. Constraints:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(...{0,2}\\.?$)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern((?s).*\\S.*)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern((?s).*\\S.*)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)` (no format check here)\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email` (optional)\n   - `registrationDate` \u2014 optional; `sharesHousehold` \u2014 unconstrained, request-only\n\n   Note: the `Owner` **entity's** own constraints (`@NotEmpty`, telephone `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)`, etc.) are **not** enforced on this path \u2014 nothing validates the entity before save, and there are no `@PrePersist`/entity-listener/auditing hooks.\n\n## Inside the controller body (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, lines 112\u2013154), in order\n\n3. **Map** DTO \u2192 new `Owner` (MapStruct; no trimming). *(side-effect: object creation)*\n4. **Normalize address** (`normalizeAddress`): trim \u2192 collapse inner whitespace \u2192 uppercase \u2192 expand street abbreviations (ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE). If empty \u2192 **400**. Then `setAddress`. *(validation + side-effect on the field)*\n5. **Normalize email** (only if non-null): trim \u2192 lowercase \u2192 match `EMAIL_PATTERN`. No match \u2192 **400**. Then `setEmail`. *(validation + side-effect)*\n6. **Normalize telephone** (`normalizeTelephone`): strip spaces/dashes/brackets; if not `+`-prefixed, drop one leading `0` and prefix `+61`; must match E.164 `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$` else returns null \u2192 **400**. Then `setTelephone`. *(validation + side-effect)*\n7. **Resolve registration date** (`resolveRegistrationDate`): use supplied date else `LocalDate.now()`, then roll weekends forward to Monday. `setRegistrationDate`. *(side-effect)*\n8. **Per-day limit**: `countOwnersRegisteredOn(date) >= 100` \u2192 **429**. *(loads all owners)*\n9. **Telephone uniqueness**: `isTelephoneInUse` \u2192 **409**. *(loads all owners)*\n10. **Household conflict**: unless `sharesHousehold == true`, if an existing owner shares normalized last name + address \u2192 **409**. *(loads all owners)*\n11. **Per-city cap**: `countOwnersInCity(city) >= 50` \u2192 **409**. *(loads all owners)*\n12. **Derive `customerCode`**: `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, NNNN = city count + 1. `setCustomerCode`. *(loads all owners; side-effect)*\n13. **Derive `membershipNumber`**: `<customerCode>-M<YY>`. `setMembershipNumber`. *(side-effect)*\n14. **Derive `householdId`**: SHA-256 of normalized lastName + address, first 12 bytes hex. `setHouseholdId`. *(side-effect)*\n15. **Derive `namesakeCount`**: count existing owners sharing normalized first+last name. `setNamesakeCount`. *(loads all owners; side-effect)*\n16. **Persist**: `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2014 `@Transactional`, `repository.save` (persist). *(the DB write)*\n17. **Map** entity \u2192 `OwnerDto`, **set `Location`** header to `/api/owners/{id}`, return **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Notable structural points\n\n- **No single transaction spans the method** \u2014 `addOwner` is not `@Transactional`. Each `findAllOwners` read and the final `saveOwner` run in their own transactions, so the uniqueness/count checks are **not atomic** with the insert (race-prone under concurrency).\n- `findAllOwners()` is invoked **repeatedly** (steps 8\u201315, roughly six full-table scans) rather than once.\n- Every repository call is wrapped by `CallMonitoringAspect` for JMX call-count/timing.\n- **No** event publishing, emails/notifications, caching, password encoding, or timestamp/auditing occurs on this path."
